# Single declaration of what is out of scope for every quality check.
#
# This file declares RUN-TIME scope, and it is still the only input to it:
# scripts/lib/scope.sh turns each line below into a git pathspec exclusion and
# hands the resulting file list to every check, so every check the runner invokes
# sees the same files.
#
# It is no longer the only place exclusions live. FR-013a, as amended on
# 2026-09-02, requires each check to ALSO declare its own skipped paths in its
# own configuration -- `ignores` in .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc, `ignore` in
# .yamllint.yml, `exclude` in ruff.toml, .prettierignore, and `Exclude` in
# .editorconfig-checker.json -- so that a contributor invoking a tool by hand,
# outside scripts/, gets this same scope. ShellCheck has no such mechanism at
# all; see .shellcheckrc.
#
# Six declarations can disagree where one could not, so scripts/lint-scope.sh
# compares them against this file and fails naming the difference. Keep them in
# step: an exclusion added here and nowhere else will fail that check.
#
# See specs/001-quality-gate-plugin/spec.md FR-013, FR-013a, FR-013b, FR-013c.
#
# One path or glob per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# Version control internals
.git

# Spec Kit's generated and vendored parts. Content this repository does not own
# and cannot fix without editing a tool. Narrowed from a wholesale `.specify`
# exclusion on 2026-09-02: FR-027 puts the extensions' per-item artifacts in
# scope, and the constitution is authored here rather than generated, so
# excluding the whole directory was excluding this repository's own writing.
.specify/scripts
.specify/templates
.specify/integrations
.specify/workflows
.specify/extensions

# Spec Kit's own generated state files. Written and rewritten by the tool, so
# formatting them would be undone on its next write -- the same reason
# LEAN-CTX.md is excluded below.
.specify/.gitignore
.specify/init-options.json
.specify/integration.json
.specify/memory/.constitution-template.json

# In scope, deliberately, and listed here only to say so: .specify/memory/
# constitution.md is authored here; .specify/extensions.yml carries the hook
# ranks this repository maintains by hand (FR-025); .specify/assessments/ and
# .specify/bugs/ hold authored per-item artifacts (FR-027). All are held to the
# same standards as every other document here.

# Claude Code consumer-side state in its entirety: generated skills, hook logs,
# machine-local settings, scratch prompts. The plugin's own authored content
# lives in top-level skills/, commands/ and agents/ -- see
# specs/001-quality-gate-plugin/research.md section 10 -- so nothing this
# repository authors is lost by excluding the whole directory.
.claude

# Owned and regenerated by the lean-ctx tool: the file carries its own
# `lean-ctx-owned` marker, and edits to satisfy a linter would be overwritten.
LEAN-CTX.md

# Agent memory
.remember

# Dependency directories, fetched rather than authored
node_modules
.venv
venv

# Tool caches
.ruff_cache
__pycache__

# Self-test fixtures: deliberately non-conforming by design, so the aggregate
# check must never see them. Also in .gitignore -- both are required.
.lint-selftest-tmp
